(a) Nothing herein shall be deemed to require suspension or revocation of a license, and each violation should be considered at the discretion of the city manager or designee and/or administrative hearing officer on a case by case basis. The city manager or designee and/or administrative hearing officer, in his/her discretion, shall consider the evidence, including any extenuating, aggravating or mitigation facts or circumstances that may affect or reflect upon the parties, the license, and/or the location of the business in light of this chapter.
(b) Any administrative penalties may be mitigated upon presentation of evidence that practices and procedures have been implemented to prevent future violations from occurring. Such mitigating factors may include:
(1) Attendance at a responsible alcohol sales and service (RASS) workshop by the licensee and/or managers;
(2) Implementation and components of written policies;
(3) Evidence that employees have or do not have alcohol seller/server permits;
(4) Evidence of internal "secret shopper" or internal "sting" operations and the results therefrom;
(5) Implementation and components of an employee training program;
(6) Length of time in business;
(7) Whether ID was requested;
(8) The degree to which the licensee has other procedures in place to monitor its alcohol servers/sellers for compliance;
(9) Whether the licensee enforces a zero-tolerance policy in which employees are terminated for any knowing violation of this chapter; and
(10) Other evidence demonstrating the licensee's efforts to comply with the ordinance and prevent illegal alcohol sales or service in the licensed establishment and the community at large.
(Ord. No. 2021-11-33, Exh. A, 11-15-2021; Ord. No. 2025-06-18, 6-9-2025)

